    -> Sort: sbtest1.id, limit input to 7 row(s) per chunk  (cost=2.26 rows=10)
        -> Filter: ((sbtest1.k in (110,111,112)) and (sbtest1.k2 in (111,112,113)))  (cost=2.26 rows=10)
            -> Covering index range scan on sbtest1 using k_1 over (k = 110 AND k2 = 111 pushed_limit 7) OR (k = 110 AND k2 = 112 pushed_limit 7) OR (7 more)  (cost=2.26 rows=10)

